# Python Development Rules

## Virtual Environment
- All Python-related operations SHALL use a virtual environment
- Never attempt to use the system pip
- Never attempt to install Python packages to the system
- The Python virtual environment SHALL be named `venv_{project}`

## Virtual Environment Tools
- All Makefile references to pip and Python installed tools SHALL use full paths to venv bin directory
- Examples:
  - `venv_{project}/bin/pytest`
  - `venv_{project}/bin/pip`

## Code Style

### Type Checking
- All Python scripts SHALL use full mypy typing
- Ensure type annotations are complete and accurate

### Documentation
- All Python scripts SHALL be documented to meet numpy style guidelines
- Follow numpy docstring conventions for functions, classes, and modules
